Description: Quick: let an item's clip node follow a changed clip rectangle
 .
 When an item that already clips is marked as having a changed clip, the scene
 graph set the new rectangle with QSGClipNode::setClipRect() and called
 QQuickDefaultClipNode::update(), which rebuilds the node's geometry only from
 the rectangle given to QQuickDefaultClipNode::setRect(). The geometry and the
 dirty state stayed those of the old rectangle, so renderers that clip by the
 geometry kept the old one, and the software renderer, which is told of the
 change by the dirty geometry, too. Set it with setRect(), as a size change
 already does.
